 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:14.0pt' lang=3Den-US>=
<span
 style=3D'font-weight:bold'>Installation cmd for Jenkins:</span></p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:14.0pt' lang=3Den-US>=
&nbsp;</p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:14.0pt' lang=3Den-US>=
<span
 style=3D'font-weight:bold'>Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (Long time support)</span></p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:14.0pt' lang=3Den-US>=
&nbsp;</p>
 <p style=3D'margin-top:18pt;margin-bottom:9pt;font-family:"Google Sans";
 font-size:15.0pt'>Step 1: Install Java (Prerequisite)</p>
 <p style=3D'margin-top:9pt;margin-bottom:12pt;font-family:"Google Sans";
 font-size:12.0pt'><span lang=3Den-IN>Jenkins is built on Java and requires=
 the
 Java Runtime Environment (JRE). </span><span style=3D'font-weight:bold'
 lang=3Den-US>OpenJDK 21</span><span lang=3Den-IN> or </span><span
 style=3D'font-weight:bold' lang=3Den-US>OpenJDK 17</span><span lang=3Den-I=
N> are
 recommended for modern Jenkins versions.</span><span lang=3Den-US> [</span=
><a
 href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DkAlNnULcMAY"><span lang=3Den-US>=
1</span></a><span
 lang=3Den-US>, </span><a
 href=3D"https://discourse.ubuntu.com/t/install-and-configure-the-jenkins-b=
uild-server/24525"><span
 lang=3Den-US>2</span></a><span lang=3Den-US>, </span><a
 href=3D"https://www.jenkins.io/doc/book/installing/linux/"><span lang=3Den=
-US>3</span></a><span
 lang=3Den-US>]</span></p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:"Google Sans";font-size:15.0pt'>bash</p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:"Google Sans";font-size:10.5pt'><span
 lang=3Den-US>sudo apt update<br>
  sudo apt install -y fontconfig openjdk-</span><span lang=3Den-IN>21-jre</=
span></p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:14.0pt' lang=3Den-US>=
&nbsp;</p>
 <p style=3D'margin-top:18pt;margin-bottom:9pt;font-family:"Google Sans";
 font-size:15.0pt'>Step 2: Add the Jenkins Repository</p>
 <p style=3D'margin-top:9pt;margin-bottom:12pt;font-family:"Google Sans";
 font-size:12.0pt'><span lang=3Den-IN>Download the official Jenkins GPG sig=
ning
 key and add the LTS (Long-Term Support) package repository to your system
 sources:</span><span lang=3Den-US> [</span><a
 href=3D"https://discourse.ubuntu.com/t/install-and-configure-the-jenkins-b=
uild-server/24525"><span
 lang=3Den-US>1</span></a><span lang=3Den-US>, </span><a
 href=3D"https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-01-15-install-configure-jenki=
ns-ubuntu/view"><span
 lang=3Den-US>2</span></a><span lang=3Den-US>]</span></p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:"Google Sans";font-size:15.0pt'>bash</p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:"Google Sans";font-size:10.5pt'><span
 lang=3Den-US># Download and add the GPG key</span><span lang=3Den-IN><br>
  curl -fsSL </span><a
 href=3D"https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io-2026.key"><span
 lang=3Den-IN>https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io-2026.key</spa=
n></a><span
 lang=3Den-IN> | sudo tee \<br>
  <span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'> 
 </span>/usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc &gt; /dev/null</span></p>
 <p style=3D'margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:10pt;font-family:"Google Sans";
 font-size:10.5pt'># Append the Jenkins repository to sources.list<br>
  echo &quot;deb [signed-by=3D/usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc] \<br>
  <span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span><a
 href=3D"https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable%20binary/">https://pkg.jenkin=
s.io/debian-stable
 binary/</a>&quot; | sudo tee \<br>
  <span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>/etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkin=
s.list
 &gt; /dev/null</p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:14.0pt' lang=3Den-US>=
&nbsp;</p>
 <p style=3D'margin-top:18pt;margin-bottom:9pt;font-family:"Google Sans";
 font-size:15.0pt'>Step 3: Install Jenkins</p>
 <p style=3D'margin-top:9pt;margin-bottom:12pt;font-family:"Google Sans";
 font-size:12.0pt'><span lang=3Den-IN>Update your package listings to inclu=
de the
 new repository and execute the installation command:</span><span lang=3Den=
-US> [</span><a
 href=3D"https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-01-15-install-configure-jenki=
ns-ubuntu/view"><span
 lang=3Den-US>1</span></a><span lang=3Den-US>]</span></p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:"Google Sans";font-size:15.0pt'>bash</p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:"Google Sans";font-size:10.5pt' lang=3D=
en-US>sudo
 apt update<br>
  sudo apt install -y jenkins</p>
 <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:14.0pt' lang=3Den-US>=
&nbsp;</p>
 <p style=3D'margin-top:18pt;margin-bottom:9pt;font-family:"Google Sans";
 font-size:15.0pt'>Step 4: Start and Enable the Jenkins Service</p>
 <p style=3D'margin-top:9pt;margin-bottom:12pt;font-family:"Google Sans";
 font-size:12.0pt'><span lang=3Den-IN>Configure systemd to start the Jenkins
 daemon right away and ensure it boots automatically whenever the server
 restarts:</span><span lang=3Den-US> [</span><a
 href=3D"https://gist.github.com/NotHarshhaa/f5ded6760305c734d562c743f7a53d=
46"><span
 lang=3Den-US>1</span></a><span lang=3Den-US>, </span><a
